# WEAR IT BETTER — COMPLETE WEBSITE REVAMP (LIGHT GRADIENT THEME, FULLY RESPONSIVE)

Build a complete, production-ready e-commerce website for "Wear It Better", a luxury brand selling handcrafted menswear and an in-house line of artisanal perfumes. This is a full revamp of an existing site. The entire site must use a LIGHT, airy, premium colour scheme enriched with elegant soft GRADIENTS, look like a high-end fashion studio designed it (not a generic template), be fully responsive on every screen size from 320px phones to 2560px monitors, and every button, link and interaction must be fully functional.

==================================================
1. TECH STACK (follow exactly)
==================================================
- React 18 + TypeScript + Vite + Tailwind CSS.
- lucide-react for icons and framer-motion for animation. No other UI libraries.
- File structure:
  - index.html, index.tsx, App.tsx, index.css
  - types.ts (Product, CartItem, Currency, etc.)
  - constants.ts (products, categories, testimonials, FAQs, currency rates, nav data)
  - context/StoreContext.tsx (cart, wishlist, currency, recent searches, toasts — persisted to localStorage)
  - hooks/useScrollState.ts ({ isScrolled, progress }), hooks/useScrollSpy.ts, hooks/useReveal.ts, hooks/useLockBody.ts, hooks/useMediaQuery.ts
  - components/ — one file per section and per UI piece
- Include package.json, vite.config.ts, tailwind.config, postcss.config and vercel.json so the project runs with `npm install && npm run build` and deploys to Vercel with zero environment variables. No API keys, no backend.

