3. LIGHT DESIGN SYSTEM
==================================================
The whole site is light. No black or dark section backgrounds anywhere (no dark hero, no dark footer, no dark mobile menu). Contrast comes from typography, warm neutrals, soft gradients, soft shadows and gold accents.

3.1 Base colors (define as Tailwind theme tokens)
- Ivory #FBF8F3 — main page background
- Porcelain #FFFFFF — cards, drawers, modals, navbar glass base
- Sand #F3EDE3 — alternating section backgrounds
- Linen #EAE2D5 — borders, dividers, input outlines
- Champagne #E9D7AE — soft gold tints, highlights, hover backgrounds
- Blush #F4E1DA — soft rose tint used inside gradients
- Mist #E6ECEA — soft sage-grey tint used inside gradients
- Gold #B08A3E — primary accent
- Deep gold #8A6A2B — gold TEXT on light backgrounds (meets contrast)
- Rose gold #C99283 — secondary accent in gradients
- Charcoal #2B2621 — headings and body text (never pure black)
- Taupe #7A6F63 — secondary text, captions
- Rosewood #9C4A4F — rare accent (sale/"Almost gone" badges, error states)

3.2 GRADIENT SYSTEM (define every gradient as a named CSS variable / Tailwind utility and reuse them consistently)
- --grad-gold (primary buttons, cart badge, progress bars, active indicators):
  linear-gradient(135deg, #B08A3E 0%, #D4B06A 50%, #E9D7AE 100%)
- --grad-gold-hover (button hover state — shift, don't jump):
  linear-gradient(135deg, #9C7832 0%, #C9A257 50%, #DCC08A 100%)
  Implement the hover with background-size: 200% and animated background-position so the gradient flows smoothly.
- --grad-rose-gold (fragrance "For Her" badges, accents, decorative shapes):
  linear-gradient(135deg, #C99283 0%, #E4B9A8 50%, #F4E1DA 100%)
- --grad-heading (gradient TEXT for H1/H2 headings — use sparingly, max one heading per section):
  linear-gradient(120deg, #2B2621 0%, #5A4630 45%, #8A6A2B 100%) with background-clip: text. Must still pass AA contrast; never apply to body text.
- --grad-hero (hero background — soft mesh effect):
  layered radial gradients: radial-gradient(at 15% 20%, #F4E1DA 0px, transparent 50%), radial-gradient(at 85% 15%, #E9D7AE 0px, transparent 45%), radial-gradient(at 70% 85%, #E6ECEA 0px, transparent 50%), base #FBF8F3. The blobs drift very slowly (30s loop) for a living, silky feel.
- --grad-section-warm (alternating section backgrounds):
  linear-gradient(180deg, #FBF8F3 0%, #F3EDE3 100%)
- --grad-section-cool (some sections for variety):
  linear-gradient(180deg, #FBF8F3 0%, #EEF1EE 100%)
- --grad-champagne-panel (newsletter panel, Discovery Set banner, promo blocks):
  linear-gradient(120deg, #F4E1DA 0%, #F3E6CC 50%, #E9D7AE 100%)
- --grad-card-surface (cards and frosted panels):
  linear-gradient(160deg, rgba(255,255,255,0.95) 0%, rgba(251,248,243,0.85) 100%)
- --grad-border (1px gradient borders on featured cards, navbar pill, focused inputs, modals):
  conic or linear gradient #B08A3E → #E9D7AE → #C99283 at ~45% opacity, implemented with a mask or padding-box/border-box technique.
- --grad-image-overlay (caption areas on images, keeps text readable):
  linear-gradient(180deg, transparent 40%, rgba(251,248,243,0.92) 100%)
- --grad-footer:
  linear-gradient(180deg, #F3EDE3 0%, #EFE4D3 100%)
- --grad-shimmer (skeleton loaders while images load):
  linear-gradient(90deg, #F3EDE3 0%, #FBF8F3 50%, #F3EDE3 100%) animated left to right.

Gradient rules:
- Gradients must feel soft, silky and luxurious — never neon, never harsh rainbow, never high-saturation.
- Every gradient stays within the light palette above; text on any gradient must meet WCAG AA.
- Use gradients with purpose: primary actions, key headings, hero, featured blocks and section rhythm. Keep product photos, body text areas and forms calm.
- Decorative elements: a few large, blurred gradient orbs (gold, rose and mist, filter: blur(80px), ~30% opacity) placed behind the hero, Atelier and newsletter sections, positioned so they never cause horizontal scroll.
- Gradient dividers: thin 1px lines fading from transparent → gold → transparent between major sections.
- Icons: thin-line icons can use a gold gradient stroke via an SVG linearGradient.

3.3 Buttons
- Primary: --grad-gold background, charcoal text, fully rounded, soft gold glow on hover (0 10px 30px -10px rgba(176,138,62,0.45)), smooth flowing gradient shift on hover, slight lift.
- Secondary: transparent with --grad-border outline and charcoal text; on hover fills with --grad-champagne-panel.
- Text links: deep-gold with a gradient underline that draws in from the left.

3.4 Shadows: soft and warm only, e.g. 0 12px 40px -16px rgba(120,90,40,0.18). No heavy grey shadows.

3.5 Typography (Google Fonts)
- "Cormorant Garamond" (400/500/600 + italic) for headings; "Manrope" (400/500/600) for body and UI.
- Fluid type with clamp(): H1 clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 5.5rem), H2 clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.5rem), body clamp(0.95rem, 1vw + 0.6rem, 1.0625rem). Body line length under 72 characters, line-height 1.65.

3.6 Layout
- Alternate --grad-section-warm, --grad-section-cool and plain Ivory backgrounds for rhythm; mix full-bleed imagery, asymmetric image/text splits and product grids. Generous whitespace. Don't make every section identical rounded cards.
- Radius hierarchy: buttons/pills fully rounded, product images 16px, large feature panels 24px.
- Subtle paper-grain overlay (CSS/SVG noise ~3% opacity) on Ivory sections.

3.7 Images
- Unsplash URLs (images.unsplash.com/...?w=900&q=80&auto=format), bright, light-toned photography — cream and neutral backdrops, natural daylight, beige/ivory/light-grey tailoring, perfume bottles on stone, linen or marble. Avoid dark, moody photos. NEVER show third-party brand logos or bottles (no Chanel, Dior, Tom Ford, etc.).
- <SmartImage> component: lazy loading, fixed aspect ratio, srcset (400/800/1200/1600), --grad-shimmer skeleton while loading, soft fade-in, and an onError fallback (--grad-champagne-panel with a gold "W" monogram) so no image ever looks broken.

