5. NAVBAR (signature element: sticky, light glass, premium)
==================================================
It must feel like the navigation of a high-end fashion house: smooth, precise and alive, never noisy.

5.1 Scroll behaviour (always visible, never hides)
- position: fixed; z-index above everything except modals, drawers and the loader. Sits directly below the announcement bar, then attaches to top: 0 once scrolled.
- STATE 1 — top of page (scrollY < 24px): full-width, transparent background, charcoal text, no border. Height 88px desktop / 72px mobile.
- STATE 2 — scrolled (scrollY ≥ 24px): morph (Framer Motion spring, stiffness 260, damping 30) into a FLOATING LIGHT GLASS PILL:
  - max-width 1180px, centred, margin-top 12px, border-radius 9999px (tablet/mobile: inset 10px each side, radius 20px).
  - Frosted light glass: background linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(255,255,255,0.72), rgba(251,248,243,0.6)), backdrop-filter: blur(18px) saturate(160%) with -webkit- prefix.
  - 1px animated --grad-border (gold → champagne → rose gold) at ~45% opacity; conic-gradient slowly rotating on an 8s loop.
  - Shadow: 0 10px 40px -12px rgba(120,90,40,0.22), 0 2px 8px rgba(43,38,33,0.06).
  - Height 64px (mobile 58px); logo scales 1 → 0.85; wordmark fades out leaving the monogram.
  - Width, radius, margin, height and logo scale animate together as one shape — never a jump.
- Scrolling back to the top morphs back to State 1.
- Over full-bleed image areas, add a subtle white-to-transparent gradient behind the State 1 bar so charcoal text stays readable.
- Use useScroll + useMotionValueEvent (or rAF-throttled listener). No layout thrashing.

5.2 Desktop (≥ 1024px)
- LEFT: logo. A soft gold-to-rose gradient glow ring behind the monogram pulses every few seconds. Hover: monogram rotates 8°, glow brightens. Click: smooth scroll to top.
- CENTRE links: Menswear, Fragrances, Atelier, Reviews, Contact.
  - Hover: a champagne-gradient glass pill glides behind the hovered link (Framer Motion layoutId).
  - Active section (scroll spy): --grad-heading gradient text + small 2px --grad-gold dot beneath.
  - "Menswear" → MEGA MENU on hover/focus (120ms hover-intent): white glass panel with --grad-border, fade + scale 0.98 → 1. Left: 3 category cards with photo, name and item count (Kurtas & Waistcoats, Suits & Jackets, Kameez Shalwar) — click scrolls to the shop and applies the filter; "View all menswear" link. Right: featured product card on --grad-champagne-panel (Ivory Silk Kurta & Waistcoat Set, price in selected currency) with working "Quick view".
  - "Fragrances" → smaller dropdown: For Him, For Her, Unisex, Discovery Set — each with a gradient icon and "from $145" (converted). Click scrolls to fragrances and applies the filter.
- RIGHT:
  - Currency selector (USD / GBP / EUR / PKR), compact glass dropdown.
  - Search button "Search ⌘K" (Ctrl K on Windows) → full-screen COMMAND SEARCH: --grad-hero frosted backdrop, large input with --grad-border focus ring and animated typing placeholder ("Search oud, kurta, waistcoat…"), instant results grouped into Menswear / Fragrances / Scent notes, arrow-key navigation, Enter opens quick view, Esc closes, recent searches, empty state "No matches — try 'oud' or 'kurta'".
  - Wishlist heart with --grad-rose-gold count badge → wishlist drawer.
  - Cart icon with --grad-gold count badge (charcoal number). On add: badge pops (1 → 1.4 → 1), icon shakes slightly, a gold gradient glow ring ripples out. Hover: mini preview (last 3 items, subtotal, "View bag"). Click: cart drawer.
  - "Sign in" text link, gradient underline draws in from the left → demo sign-in modal (validation, "Demo only" note).
  - "Book a fitting" pill: --grad-gold, light shine sweep every 6s, magnetic hover (max 6px), flowing gradient + lift + soft glow on hover. Scrolls to Book a Fitting.
- 2px --grad-gold SCROLL PROGRESS BAR along the navbar's bottom edge (inside the pill when floating, clipped to its rounded ends).

5.3 Small laptop (1024–1279px): reduce link gaps, move "Sign in" into an account icon, keep everything on one line with no wrapping.

5.4 Tablet (768–1023px): logo left; links condensed to Menswear, Fragrances, Atelier; search, cart and hamburger right. "Book a fitting" becomes a compact icon + "Fitting" gradient pill.

5.5 Mobile (< 768px) — must be flawless
- Bar: monogram left; search, cart (badge) and hamburger right. Tap targets ≥ 44×44px. Light glass pill when scrolled (inset 10px, radius 20px), respecting env(safe-area-inset-top).
- HAMBURGER: two charcoal lines morphing smoothly into an X.
- MOBILE MENU: full-screen LIGHT overlay with --grad-hero background (slowly drifting gold, rose and mist gradient blobs) and faint paper grain, revealed by a circular clip-path expanding from the hamburger.
  - Large Cormorant Garamond links (~40px, charcoal) stagger in from below 60ms apart, each with a small taupe index number (01, 02, 03…).
  - Tapping a link: quick champagne gradient highlight, menu closes with reverse clip-path, then smooth-scrolls to the section.
  - Below: swipeable row of category chips with --grad-border (Kurtas, Waistcoats, Suits, For Him, For Her, Unisex — each applies its filter; active chip fills with --grad-gold), currency selector, "Sign in", full-width --grad-gold "Book a fitting" button, social icons (Instagram, Facebook, YouTube).
  - Lock body scroll; close on Esc, swipe-down or link tap; return focus to the hamburger. Content scrolls internally on short screens (landscape phones).
- MOBILE BOTTOM ACTION BAR: after scrolling past the hero, a floating white gradient-glass bar with --grad-border slides up with Home, Shop, Wishlist (badge), Bag (badge); active icon uses a gold gradient. Respects env(safe-area-inset-bottom); hides while any drawer, search or the mobile menu is open. Add bottom page padding so it never covers content.

5.6 Entrance: after the loader, navbar enters from above (y -24 → 0, opacity 0 → 1); logo, links, then right-side buttons stagger in 40ms apart.

5.7 Accessibility
- Semantic <header> and <nav aria-label="Main">; aria-expanded/aria-controls on hamburger and dropdowns; "Skip to content" as the first focusable element.
- Full keyboard support (Tab, focus-open dropdowns, arrow keys in menus, Esc closes all). Visible deep-gold focus rings. WCAG AA contrast in every state.
- prefers-reduced-motion: keep glass/colour/gradient changes, replace morphing, sliding, shine, magnetic, drifting blobs and rotating border with simple fades.
- No backdrop-filter support → solid rgba(255,255,255,0.96).
- Components: Navbar, NavLinks, MegaMenu, FragranceDropdown, CommandSearch, CartButton, CurrencySelect, MobileMenu, MobileBottomBar.

