10. FULL RESPONSIVENESS (critical — test every size)
==================================================
The site must look intentionally designed at EVERY width, not just stretch or squash.

Breakpoints and targets:
- 320–374px (small phones, iPhone SE): single-column everywhere except product grids (2 columns, compact cards), 16px side padding, smaller hero headline via clamp, no text overflow or cut-off buttons.
- 375–639px (standard phones): 20px side padding; product grids 2 columns; stacked CTAs; bottom action bar active.
- 640–767px (large phones / small tablets portrait): 24px padding; collections still carousel; testimonials 1 card with peek.
- 768–1023px (tablets): 32px padding; menswear 3 columns, fragrances 2; split sections stack image over text; tablet navbar.
- 1024–1279px (small laptops): 40px padding; menswear 4 columns, fragrances 3; compact desktop navbar.
- 1280–1535px (laptops/desktops): container max-width 1280px.
- 1536–2560px (large and ultra-wide): container max-width 1440px, centered; type scales up via clamp but caps out; gradient backgrounds and orbs extend full width while content stays contained; never stretch content edge to edge except intentional full-bleed images.

Rules:
- Mobile-first Tailwind classes; fluid spacing and type with clamp().
- No horizontal scroll at any width (overflow-x: clip on html/body; check every carousel, marquee, gradient orb, mega menu and modal).
- Gradient orbs scale down and reduce blur on mobile for performance.
- Use 100svh/100dvh instead of 100vh so mobile browser bars don't cut content.
- Landscape phones (e.g. 844×390): hero, mobile menu, modals and drawers must still fit and scroll internally.
- Images: responsive srcset/sizes, consistent aspect ratios (products 4:5, collections 3:4, hero adaptive), object-fit: cover, never distorted.
- Touch targets ≥ 44px; inputs at 16px font to prevent iOS zoom; no hover-only functionality on touch devices.
- Respect safe-area insets (notches, home indicator) on navbar, bottom bar, drawers and modals.
- Text never overflows: long product names wrap or clamp to 2 lines; prices and buttons never collide.
- Modals become bottom sheets or full-screen on mobile; drawers become full-width under 480px.
- Test in Chrome, Safari (iOS and macOS), Firefox and Edge (include -webkit- prefixes for background-clip: text and backdrop-filter).

